%language Git commit

# The subject is a heading; a Conventional Commits prefix, its type a
# keyword; the body plain
> Fix the parse of a deleted SQL comment
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.heading
>
> The grammar read `--- x` as a file's name.
  ^^^ -

# The prefix's type, its scope a parameter
> fix(diff)!: read a deleted line
  ^^^ keyword
      ^^^^ variable.parameter
              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.heading

# A trailer's token is a label, `BREAKING CHANGE:` a keyword
> Subject
>
> BREAKING CHANGE: the diff grammar comes from git now
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ keyword
> Signed-off-by: A Dev <dev@example.com>
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ label

# git's comments are comments, with the branch named in them; they are
# known by the whole of what git writes, its first lines too
> Subject
> # Please enter the commit message for your changes. Lines starting
> # with '#' will be ignored, and an empty message aborts the commit.
> #
> # On branch master
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^ comment
              ^^^^^^ constant
> # Changes to be committed:
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.heading

# Below the scissors `git commit -v` writes the diff, which is a diff's
> Subject
> # ------------------------ >8 ------------------------
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ comment
> # Do not modify or remove the line above.
> # Everything below it will be ignored.
> diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ keyword
> --- a/Cargo.toml
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ diff.minus
> +++ b/Cargo.toml
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ diff.plus
> @@ -1 +1 @@
> -old = 1
  ^^^^^^^^ diff.minus
> +new = 2
  ^^^^^^^^ diff.plus

# A merge's message as git writes it: the subject a heading, the help a
# comment
> Merge branch 'feature'
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.heading
> # Please enter a commit message to explain why this merge is necessary,
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ comment

# A squash's message: the commands done are a rebase's, in the comments
> # This is a combination of 2 commits.
> # This is the 1st commit message:
>
> second
  ^^^^^^ markup.heading
>
> # This is the commit message #2:
>
> # fixup! second
>
> # Please enter the commit message for your changes. Lines starting
> # with '#' will be ignored, and an empty message aborts the commit.
> #
> # interactive rebase in progress; onto ec3b0de
                                         ^^^^^^^ constant
> # Last commands done (2 commands done):
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.heading
> #    pick 0e0be44 # second
       ^^^^ keyword
            ^^^^^^^ constant.builtin
> #    squash c2af15e # fixup! second
       ^^^^^^ keyword
> # No commands remaining.
